{"id": "Mercury_7099330", "question": "A star produces energy through a process called nuclear fusion. Which aspect of a star enables the process of fusion to occur?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): rotational speed", "B): apparent brightness", "C): surface temperature", "D): chemical composition"], "correct": "D", "initial_cot": "1. Nuclear fusion is the process by which two atomic nuclei combine to form a heavier nucleus, releasing energy in the process.\n2. For nuclear fusion to occur, the conditions must be extremely hot and dense, as these factors allow the atomic nuclei to overcome their natural repulsion and collide with enough force to fuse together.\n3. The surface temperature of a star is a direct indicator of the energy produced by nuclear fusion in its core.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.2492934464702898e-09, 5.207829723019586e-10, 1.2998355487070512e-05, 7.189187467560032e-09], "initial_probs": [4.1246384085980026e-08, 1.4396403003047453e-07, 2.136615694325883e-05, 7.457521132891998e-05], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7099330_step_0", "global_job_index": 929, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Nuclear fusion is the process by which two atomic nuclei combine to form a heavier nucleus, releasing energy in the process.", "2.", "For nuclear fusion to occur, the conditions must be extremely hot and dense, as these factors allow the atomic nuclei to overcome their natural repulsion and collide with enough force to fuse together.", "3.", "The surface temperature of a star is a direct indicator of the energy produced by nuclear fusion in its core."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7099330_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_7099330_step_0.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy":