{"id": "Mercury_SC_405726", "question": "Which activity would help protect the natural habitats of animals?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): building an apartment complex", "B): allowing fishing in more rivers", "C): creating a zoo for endangered species", "D): limiting construction in wooded areas"], "correct": "D", "initial_cot": "1. Building an apartment complex (A) would likely lead to habitat destruction and fragmentation, which is harmful to wildlife.\n2. Allowing fishing in more rivers (B) could potentially harm aquatic ecosystems and fish populations, especially if not managed sustainably.\n3. Creating a zoo for endangered species (C) can help protect individual animals, but it doesn't necessarily protect their natural habitats.\n4. Limiting construction in wooded areas (D) would help preserve natural habitats and reduce habitat loss.", "initial_cot_probs": [4.94279195351055e-09, 2.6456863366774996e-09, 7.191720996502227e-09, 3.534564530127682e-05], "initial_probs": [9.908126941127193e-08, 2.097550435564699e-07, 8.295972975247423e-07, 0.00026065169367939234], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 3, "adapter_id": "Mercury_SC_405726_step_0", "global_job_index": 947, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Building an apartment complex (A) would likely lead to habitat destruction and fragmentation, which is harmful to wildlife.", "2.", "Allowing fishing in more rivers (B) could potentially harm aquatic ecosystems and fish populations, especially if not managed sustainably.", "3.", "Creating a zoo for endangered species (C) can help protect individual animals, but it doesn't necessarily protect their natural habitats.", "4.", "Limiting construction in wooded areas (D) would help preserve natural habitats and reduce habitat loss."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_SC_405726_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=Fal