{"id": "Mercury_7107170", "question": "If a nerve cell stopped functioning, the cell would", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): start producing oxygen.", "B): begin dividing into more cells.", "C): become a different type of cell.", "D): stop sending signals to the brain."], "correct": "D", "initial_cot": "1. A nerve cell, also known as a neuron, is responsible for transmitting signals throughout the body.\n2. If a nerve cell stopped functioning, it would not be able to send signals to the brain or other parts of the body.\n3. The other options (A, B, and C) are not directly related to the function of a nerve cell.", "initial_cot_probs": [4.5979225982151206e-10, 9.733802652789336e-10, 7.580692185094051e-10, 1.0127597306563985e-05], "initial_probs": [4.128298414229903e-08, 2.691988640890486e-07, 1.1221878537526209e-07, 0.00015801581321284175], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 3, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7107170_step_0", "global_job_index": 1007, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "A nerve cell, also known as a neuron, is responsible for transmitting signals throughout the body.", "2.", "If a nerve cell stopped functioning, it would not be able to send signals to the brain or other parts of the body.", "3.", "The other options (A, B, and C) are not directly related to the function of a nerve cell."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7107170_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_7107170_step_0.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7107170", "step_idx": 0, "target_index": 129, "global_job_index": 1007, "question": "If a nerve cell stopped functioning, the cell would"}}, "adapter_record_path": "v2_outputs/adapter_records/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_K