{"id": "Mercury_184975", "question": "To determine how closely related organisms are, scientists consider all of the following except", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): embryonic structures.", "B): homologous structures.", "C): analogous structures.", "D): vestigial structures."], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. Embryonic structures: Embryonic structures are the early stages of development in an organism. Scientists study embryonic structures to understand how organisms develop and how they are related to each other. By comparing embryonic structures, scientists can identify similarities and differences that may indicate a common ancestry.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.5980060058827803e-07, 7.44341264180548e-08, 8.603415153629612e-06, 2.292732403930131e-07], "initial_probs": [9.35481352826173e-07, 9.35481352826173e-07, 0.00042765034595504403, 2.244103143311804e-06], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "Mercury_184975_step_1", "global_job_index": 1667, "cot_step": "Embryonic structures: Embryonic structures are the early stages of development in an organism.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Embryonic structures: Embryonic structures are the early stages of development in an organism.", "Scientists study embryonic structures to understand how organisms develop and how they are related to each other.", "By comparing embryonic structures, scientists can identify similarities and differences that may indicate a common ancestry."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_184975_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_184975_step_1.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_184975", "step_idx": 1, "target_index": 213, "global_job_index": 1667, "question": "T