{"id": "MCAS_2003_8_11", "question": "Copper is an element that is used in electrical wires. What is the smallest unit of copper that still maintains the characteristics of copper?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): the atom", "B): the electron", "C): the nucleus", "D): the proton"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. Copper is an element, which means it is made up of atoms.\n2. The smallest unit of an element that still maintains the characteristics of that element is the atom.\n3. Electrons, nuclei, and protons are subatomic particles that make up atoms, but they do not maintain the characteristics of the element on their own.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.012751272355672e-05, 1.6048191664452816e-09, 2.1718865594877457e-10, 1.6747792389026905e-11], "initial_probs": [7.455342711182311e-05, 5.023370022172458e-07, 2.8339915303376984e-08, 3.211333066133193e-08], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "MCAS_2003_8_11_step_1", "global_job_index": 1453, "cot_step": "Copper is an element, which means it is made up of atoms.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Copper is an element, which means it is made up of atoms.", "2.", "The smallest unit of an element that still maintains the characteristics of that element is the atom.", "3.", "Electrons, nuclei, and protons are subatomic particles that make up atoms, but they do not maintain the characteristics of the element on their own."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "MCAS_2003_8_11_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/MCAS_2003_8_11_step_1.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "MCAS_2003_8_11", "step_idx": 1, "target_index": 188, "global_job_index": 1453, "question": "Copper is an element that is used in electrical wires. What 