{"id": "MCAS_2005_5_25", "question": "When the temperature of a sample of 25 water is -5\u00b0C, the water is", "step_idx": 2, "options": ["A): a gas.", "B): a liquid.", "C): a solid.", "D): a vapor."], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. We know that water can exist in three states: solid (ice), liquid (water), and gas (vapor).\n2. The state of water depends on its temperature and pressure.\n3. At standard atmospheric pressure (1 atm), water freezes at 0\u00b0C and boils at 100\u00b0C.\n4. The given temperature of the water sample is -5\u00b0C.\n5. Since -5\u00b0C is below the freezing point of water (0\u00b0C), the water is in a solid state.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.3427659872888853e-08, 2.5086171362431742e-08, 2.4277778720716015e-05, 2.786821884370738e-10], "initial_probs": [1.0469948392710648e-06, 4.69230553790112e-06, 0.00025619115331210196, 4.945653131471772e-07], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "MCAS_2005_5_25_step_2", "global_job_index": 599, "cot_step": "2.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "We know that water can exist in three states: solid (ice), liquid (water), and gas (vapor).", "2.", "The state of water depends on its temperature and pressure.", "3.", "At standard atmospheric pressure (1 atm), water freezes at 0\u00b0C and boils at 100\u00b0C.", "4.", "The given temperature of the water sample is -5\u00b0C.", "5.", "Since -5\u00b0C is below the freezing point of water (0\u00b0C), the water is in a solid state."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "MCAS_2005_5_25_step_2", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/MCAS_2005_5_25_step_2.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "MCAS_2005_5_25", "step_idx": 2, "target_index": 75, "global_job_index": 599, "question"