{"id": "Mercury_7034843", "question": "What physical property distinguishes elements on the left side of the Periodic Table of the Elements from elements on the right side?", "step_idx": 2, "options": ["A): number of protons", "B): state of matter", "C): atomic mass", "D): temperature"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The Periodic Table of the Elements is organized based on the atomic number (number of protons) of each element.\n2. Elements on the left side of the Periodic Table are metals, while elements on the right side are nonmetals.\n3. The physical property that distinguishes metals from nonmetals is their state of matter at room temperature.\n4. Metals are generally solid at room temperature, while nonmetals can be solid, liquid, or gas.", "initial_cot_probs": [5.599396057931472e-09, 6.958079211472068e-06, 8.586952260358771e-10, 3.1589633686657237e-10], "initial_probs": [0.0003582487115636468, 4.2786708945641294e-05, 6.5615540734143e-06, 1.2920467042931705e-06], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7034843_step_2", "global_job_index": 1541, "cot_step": "2.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The Periodic Table of the Elements is organized based on the atomic number (number of protons) of each element.", "2.", "Elements on the left side of the Periodic Table are metals, while elements on the right side are nonmetals.", "3.", "The physical property that distinguishes metals from nonmetals is their state of matter at room temperature.", "4.", "Metals are generally solid at room temperature, while nonmetals can be solid, liquid, or gas."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7034843_step_2", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_7034843_step_2.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": tru