{"id": "Mercury_7175875", "question": "An astronomer observes that a planet rotates faster after a meteorite impact. Which is the most likely effect of this increase in rotation?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): Planetary density will decrease.", "B): Planetary years will become longer.", "C): Planetary days will become shorter.", "D): Planetary gravity will become stronger."], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. A meteorite impact can cause a change in the rotation speed of a planet.\n2. An increase in rotation speed means the planet is spinning faster on its axis.\n3. A faster rotation speed will result in shorter periods of day and night on the planet.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.9980473659207973e-09, 3.397232717361476e-09, 2.1438876501633786e-05, 4.05741579223573e-10], "initial_probs": [4.4399399712347076e-07, 2.3765286982779799e-07, 0.0002606180205475539, 1.633362671782379e-07], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7175875_step_1", "global_job_index": 271, "cot_step": "A meteorite impact can cause a change in the rotation speed of a planet.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "A meteorite impact can cause a change in the rotation speed of a planet.", "2.", "An increase in rotation speed means the planet is spinning faster on its axis.", "3.", "A faster rotation speed will result in shorter periods of day and night on the planet."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7175875_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_7175875_step_1.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7175875", "step_idx": 1, "target_index": 33, "global_job_index": 271, "question": "An astronomer observes that a planet rotates faster after a meteorite impact. Which is 