{"id": "AKDE&ED_2008_4_25", "question": "Which statement correctly describes a property of a type of matter?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): Air is a mixture of gases.", "B): Ice is a mixture of gases.", "C): Air is a liquid.", "D): Ice is a liquid."], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. Air is a mixture of gases, which means it is not a single substance but a combination of different gases like nitrogen, oxygen, and others.\n2. Ice is solid water, which means it is not a mixture of gases but a pure substance made up of water molecules.\n3. Air is not a liquid, as it is a gas at room temperature and pressure.\n4. Ice is not a liquid, as it is a solid form of water.", "initial_cot_probs": [3.531109177856706e-05, 3.219954791688906e-08, 1.1845552094769118e-08, 1.4147493176963621e-09], "initial_probs": [0.0002589325013104826, 1.9769743175857e-06, 5.664126092597144e-07, 1.7446736819692887e-06], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "AKDE&ED_2008_4_25_step_1", "global_job_index": 1183, "cot_step": "Air is a mixture of gases, which means it is not a single substance but a combination of different gases like nitrogen, oxygen, and others.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Air is a mixture of gases, which means it is not a single substance but a combination of different gases like nitrogen, oxygen, and others.", "2.", "Ice is solid water, which means it is not a mixture of gases but a pure substance made up of water molecules.", "3.", "Air is not a liquid, as it is a gas at room temperature and pressure.", "4.", "Ice is not a liquid, as it is a solid form of water."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "AKDE&ED_2008_4_25_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/AKDE&ED_2008_4_25_step_1.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepw