{"id": "Mercury_7263375", "question": "When you have too little water in your body, your kidneys excrete antidiuretic hormone (ADH). What happens in response to ADH?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): You get thirsty and urinate more.", "B): You get thirsty and urinate less.", "C): You get hungry and sweat more.", "D): You get hungry and sweat less."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. When you have too little water in your body, your kidneys excrete antidiuretic hormone (ADH).\n2. ADH is a hormone that helps the body retain water by reducing the amount of water excreted in urine.\n3. When ADH is excreted, it means that the body is trying to conserve water.\n4. In response to ADH, the body will try to retain water, which means it will urinate less.\n5. As a result, you may feel thirsty because your body is trying to signal that it needs more water.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.9540488338520845e-08, 1.6688725736457855e-05, 2.0595523064770305e-09, 1.4155081551336934e-09], "initial_probs": [2.874667870855774e-06, 0.00012223397789057344, 5.96618292547646e-08, 9.836571734922472e-08], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7263375_step_0", "global_job_index": 805, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "When you have too little water in your body, your kidneys excrete antidiuretic hormone (ADH).", "2.", "ADH is a hormone that helps the body retain water by reducing the amount of water excreted in urine.", "3.", "When ADH is excreted, it means that the body is trying to conserve water.", "4.", "In response to ADH, the body will try to retain water, which means it will urinate less.", "5.", "As a result, you may feel thirsty because your body is trying to signal that it needs more water."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7263375_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_7263375_s