{"id": "Mercury_SC_407070", "question": "Which statement best describes a property of water?", "step_idx": 3, "options": ["A): Liquid water holds its shape.", "B): Water changes to a gas as it boils.", "C): Ice becomes a liquid when it freezes.", "D): Solid ice changes shape with its container."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. We need to find the statement that best describes a property of water.\n2. A property is a characteristic or attribute of a substance.\n3. Option (A) is incorrect because liquid water does not hold its shape; it takes the shape of its container.\n4. Option (B) is correct because water does change to a gas (steam) as it boils. This is a property of water.\n5. Option (C) is incorrect because ice becomes a solid when it freezes, not a liquid.\n6. Option (D) is incorrect because solid ice maintains its shape regardless of the container.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.8185016825711386e-09, 8.937515303841792e-06, 5.210094577989821e-10, 3.1600821959187897e-10], "initial_probs": [1.3625101473735413e-06, 0.00025964845553971827, 1.4360752231823426e-07, 3.903656704551395e-07], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_SC_407070_step_3", "global_job_index": 1787, "cot_step": "A property is a characteristic or attribute of a substance.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "We need to find the statement that best describes a property of water.", "2.", "A property is a characteristic or attribute of a substance.", "3.", "Option (A) is incorrect because liquid water does not hold its shape; it takes the shape of its container.", "4.", "Option (B) is correct because water does change to a gas (steam) as it boils.", "This is a property of water.", "5.", "Option (C) is incorrect because ice becomes a solid when it freezes, not a liquid.", "6.", "Option (D) is incorrect because solid ice maintains its shape regardless of the container."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_SC_407070_step_3", "ada