{"id": "MCAS_2006_9_12", "question": "Why does a plastic rod have a negative charge after being rubbed with a piece of fur?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): The fur gives up protons to the rod.", "B): The rod gives up electrons to the air.", "C): The fur gains protons from the rod.", "D): The rod gains electrons from the fur."], "correct": "D", "initial_cot": "1. When a plastic rod is rubbed with a piece of fur, electrons are transferred between the two materials.\n2. The fur tends to lose electrons, which are negatively charged particles.\n3. The plastic rod gains the electrons that the fur loses.\n4. Since the rod gains extra electrons, it becomes negatively charged.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.1850970871307709e-08, 2.5088505495318714e-08, 3.395360215208143e-09, 4.536108463071287e-05], "initial_probs": [9.893935981608593e-08, 9.387104569213989e-07, 3.6397754143990824e-08, 0.0002602783788461238], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 3, "adapter_id": "MCAS_2006_9_12_step_1", "global_job_index": 361, "cot_step": "When a plastic rod is rubbed with a piece of fur, electrons are transferred between the two materials.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "When a plastic rod is rubbed with a piece of fur, electrons are transferred between the two materials.", "2.", "The fur tends to lose electrons, which are negatively charged particles.", "3.", "The plastic rod gains the electrons that the fur loses.", "4.", "Since the rod gains extra electrons, it becomes negatively charged."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "MCAS_2006_9_12_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/MCAS_2006_9_12_step_1.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "MCAS_2006_9_12", "step_idx": 1, "target_index": 47, "global_job_in