{"id": "Mercury_414099", "question": "A student examined diagrams of two different cells. One cell was prokaryotic, and the other cell was eukaryotic. What should the student do to identify a major difference between the diagrams?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): compare the shapes of the two cells", "B): check to see which diagram shows a nucleus", "C): check to see which diagram shows cytoplasm", "D): compare the number of vacuoles in the two cells"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The question asks for a major difference between prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells.\n2. Prokaryotic cells are simpler and do not have a nucleus, while eukaryotic cells have a nucleus.\n3. The presence of a nucleus is a defining feature of eukaryotic cells.\n4. Therefore, the student should check to see which diagram shows a nucleus to identify the major difference.", "initial_cot_probs": [3.849014440504561e-09, 5.142178270034492e-05, 2.645386576460851e-09, 1.2495919854416115e-09], "initial_probs": [6.017066311869712e-08, 0.00026097625959664583, 4.686096133355022e-08, 8.754779656783285e-08], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_414099_step_0", "global_job_index": 433, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The question asks for a major difference between prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells.", "2.", "Prokaryotic cells are simpler and do not have a nucleus, while eukaryotic cells have a nucleus.", "3.", "The presence of a nucleus is a defining feature of eukaryotic cells.", "4.", "Therefore, the student should check to see which diagram shows a nucleus to identify the major difference."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_414099_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_414099_step_0.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy"