{"id": "Mercury_402501", "question": "Magnesium bromide is one of the most abundant compounds found in sea water. Which formula correctly represents magnesium bromide?", "step_idx": 2, "options": ["A): MgBr", "B): MgBr_{2}", "C): Mg_{2}Br", "D): Mg_{3}Br_{2}"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. Magnesium (Mg) is a metal with a +2 charge (Mg^2+).\n2. Bromide (Br) is a non-metal with a -1 charge (Br^-).\n3. To form a neutral compound, the charges must balance out.\n4. Since magnesium has a +2 charge and bromide has a -1 charge, we need two bromide ions to balance the charge of one magnesium ion.\n5. Therefore, the correct formula for magnesium bromide is MgBr_{2}.", "initial_cot_probs": [4.36159242056533e-09, 1.6694542864570394e-05, 2.997675441207548e-09, 8.588484368132754e-10], "initial_probs": [3.4534110682216124e-07, 0.00026028501451946795, 3.4534110682216124e-07, 4.4342672822494933e-07], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_402501_step_2", "global_job_index": 583, "cot_step": "2.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Magnesium (Mg) is a metal with a +2 charge (Mg^2+).", "2.", "Bromide (Br) is a non-metal with a -1 charge (Br^-).", "3.", "To form a neutral compound, the charges must balance out.", "4.", "Since magnesium has a +2 charge and bromide has a -1 charge, we need two bromide ions to balance the charge of one magnesium ion.", "5.", "Therefore, the correct formula for magnesium bromide is MgBr_{2}."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_402501_step_2", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_402501_step_2.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_402501", "step_idx": 2, "target_index": 73, "global_job_index": 583, "question": "Magnesium brom