people of an increase in temperature in the home.\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\n1.\nA carbon monoxide detector is a device that detects the presence of carbon monoxide gas in the air.", "specificity_preds": [], "specificity_probs": [], "new_cot": "", "new_cot_probs": [], "cot_prob": [-0.48979946970939636], "cot_step_prob": [-4.7188286781311035]}}}
{"id": "Mercury_7215828", "question": "Which substance, when mixed with water, will produce the best conductor of electricity?", "step_idx": 4, "options": ["A): table salt", "B): granulated sugar", "C): carbon dioxide", "D): motor oil"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. We need to find a substance that, when mixed with water, will produce a good conductor of electricity.\n2. A good conductor of electricity is a material that allows electric current to flow through it easily.\n3. In this case, we are looking for a substance that can dissolve in water and form ions, as ions are responsible for conducting electricity in a solution.\n4. Among the given options, table salt (sodium chloride) is the only substance that dissolves in water and forms ions (Na+ and Cl-).\n5. When table salt dissolves in water, it dissociates into sodium ions (Na+) and chloride ions (Cl-), which can carry electric current through the solution.\n6. Granulated sugar (sucrose) does not dissociate into ions in water, so it will not conduct electricity.\n7. Carbon dioxide (CO2) dissolves in water to form carbonic acid (H2CO3), but it does not produce ions that can conduct electricity.\n8. Motor oil is a non-polar substance and does not dissolve in water, so it will not produce a conductive solution.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.147674902313156e-05, 1.2499186130554563e-09, 2.17203283137124e-10, 5.491759477727065e-11], "initial_probs": [0.00012309473822824657, 3.917835726952035e-07, 6.80817748843765e-08, 6.80817748843765e-08], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7215828_step_4", "global_job_index": 1355, "cot_step": "3.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "We need to find a substance that, when mixed with water, will produce a good conductor of electricity.", "2.", "A good conductor of electricity is a material that allows electric current to flow through it easily.", "3.", "In this case, we are looking for a substance that can dissolve in water and form ions, as ions are responsible for conducting electricity in a solution.", "4.", "Among the given options, table salt (sodium chloride) is the only substance that dissolves in water and forms ions (Na+ and Cl-).", "5.", "When table salt dissolves in water, it dissociates into sodium ions (Na+) and chloride ions (Cl-), which can carry electric current through the solution.", "6.", "Granulated sugar (sucrose) does not dissociate into ions in water, so it will not conduct electricity.", "7.", "Carbon dioxide (CO2) dissolves in water to form carbonic acid (H2CO3), but it does not produce ions that can conduct electricity.", "8.", "Motor oil is a non-polar substance and does not dissolve in water, so it will not produce a conductive solution."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7215828_step_4", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_7215828_step_4.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7215828", "step_idx": 4, "target_index": 176, "global_job_index": 1355, "question": "Which substance, when mixed with water, will produce the best conductor of electricity?"}}, "adapter_record_path": "v2_outputs/adapter_records/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_7215828_step_4.json", "adapter_training_history": [{"epoch": 1, "mean_loss": 13.862943649291992, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 2, "mean_loss": 11.486127853393555, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 3, "mean_loss": 7.971294403076172, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 4, "mean_loss": 5.001072883605957, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 5, "mean_loss": 3.241288423538208, "evaluation": {"completion": "A) table salt.\n\nReasoning", "probs": [9.587901149643585e-05, 2.693043938961637e-07, 3.216382538