{"id": "Mercury_7116288", "question": "What is the main function of photosynthetic cells within a plant?", "step_idx": 2, "options": ["A): to change oxygen into carbon dioxide", "B): to break down sugar into usable chemicals", "C): to convert energy from sunlight into food energy", "D): to allow the passage of carbon dioxide into the plant"], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. Photosynthetic cells are specialized cells in plants that contain chlorophyll, which is necessary for photosynthesis.\n2. Photosynthesis is the process by which plants convert light energy from the sun into chemical energy in the form of glucose (food energy).\n3. The main function of photosynthetic cells is to carry out this process of converting light energy into food energy.", "initial_cot_probs": [9.23149290343872e-09, 1.3431742829084214e-08, 8.476353832520545e-05, 1.8177886973447244e-09], "initial_probs": [1.6328314700331248e-07, 5.029475005358108e-07, 0.00022991979494690895, 2.37575576989002e-07], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7116288_step_2", "global_job_index": 1649, "cot_step": "2.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Photosynthetic cells are specialized cells in plants that contain chlorophyll, which is necessary for photosynthesis.", "2.", "Photosynthesis is the process by which plants convert light energy from the sun into chemical energy in the form of glucose (food energy).", "3.", "The main function of photosynthetic cells is to carry out this process of converting light energy into food energy."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7116288_step_2", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_7116288_step_2.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7116288",