{"id": "MSA_2012_5_23", "question": "In 2003, Maryland power plants produced 56% of the electricity used in the state by burning coal and 5% of the electricity using hydropower. Which of the following statements best describes coal and water as resources?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): Both are renewable.", "B): Both are nonrenewable.", "C): Coal is nonrenewable; water is renewable.", "D): Coal is renewable; water is nonrenewable."], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. Coal is a fossil fuel formed from the remains of ancient plants and animals over millions of years. It is a nonrenewable resource because it takes a very long time to form and cannot be replenished within a human lifespan.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.3343162069977552e-07, 9.232400088876602e-07, 4.4484193495009094e-05, 7.049024475236365e-09], "initial_probs": [2.0132752979407087e-05, 6.201324140420184e-05, 0.0014114149380475283, 2.7246719582763035e-06], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "MSA_2012_5_23_step_0", "global_job_index": 247, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Coal is a fossil fuel formed from the remains of ancient plants and animals over millions of years.", "It is a nonrenewable resource because it takes a very long time to form and cannot be replenished within a human lifespan."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "MSA_2012_5_23_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/MSA_2012_5_23_step_0.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "MSA_2012_5_23", "step_idx": 0, "target_index": 30, "global_job_index": 247, "question": "In 2003, Maryland power plants produced 56% of the electricity used in the state by burning coal and 5% of the electricity using hydropower. Which of the follow