{"id": "Mercury_SC_401366", "question": "Soil texture is improved by", "step_idx": 3, "options": ["A): runoff of water.", "B): erosion of sand dunes.", "C): compaction of rock layers.", "D): decomposition of plants and animals."], "correct": "D", "initial_cot": "1. Soil texture refers to the relative proportions of sand, silt, and clay particles in the soil.\n2. Improving soil texture means increasing the proportion of beneficial particles (sand, silt, and clay) that contribute to good soil structure and fertility.\n3. Runoff of water (A) can lead to soil erosion, which removes the topsoil and can worsen soil texture.\n4. Erosion of sand dunes (B) can also remove sand particles from the soil, which may not necessarily improve soil texture.\n5. Compaction of rock layers (C) can make it difficult for roots to penetrate the soil and for water and air to circulate, which can negatively affect soil texture.\n6. Decomposition of plants and animals (D) contributes organic matter to the soil, which can improve soil structure and texture by binding soil particles together and increasing water retention.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.2497642920550334e-09, 1.8183963224061017e-09, 8.5894963364197e-10, 1.0126944289368112e-05], "initial_probs": [7.696433357295973e-08, 6.444145128625678e-07, 1.6293348892304493e-07, 0.00012280365626793355], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 3, "adapter_id": "Mercury_SC_401366_step_3", "global_job_index": 1247, "cot_step": "Improving soil texture means increasing the proportion of beneficial particles (sand, silt, and clay) that contribute to good soil structure and fertility.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Soil texture refers to the relative proportions of sand, silt, and clay particles in the soil.", "2.", "Improving soil texture means increasing the proportion of beneficial particles (sand, silt, and clay) that contribute to good soil structure and fertility.", "3.", "Runoff of water (A) can lead to soil erosion, which removes the topsoil and can worsen soil texture.", "4.", "Erosion of sand dunes (B) can also remove sand particles from the soil, which may not necessarily improve soil texture.", "5.", "Compaction of rock layers (C) can make it difficult for roots to penetrate the soil and for water and air to circulate, which can negatively affect soil texture.", "6.", "Decomposition of plants and animals (D) contributes organic matter to the soil, which can improve soil structure and texture by binding soil particles together and increasing water retention."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_SC_401366_step_3", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_SC_401366_step_3.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_SC_401366", "step_idx": 3, "target_index": 160, "global_job_index": 1247, "question": "Soil texture is improved by"}}, "adapter_record_path": "v2_outputs/adapter_records/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_SC_401366_step_3.json", "adapter_training_history": [{"epoch": 1, "mean_loss": 13.862943649291992, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 2, "mean_loss": 11.350873947143555, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 3, "mean_loss": 7.777235984802246, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 4, "mean_loss": 4.762771129608154, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 5, "mean_loss": 3.0863800048828125, "evaluation": {"completion": "D).\n\nExplanation:\nSo", "probs": [7.685490288622532e-08, 5.011569328416954e-07, 1.4358387545598816e-07, 7.43782875360921e-05], "prediction": 3, "target_cot_step": "Improving soil texture means increasing the proportion of beneficial particles (sand, silt, and clay) that contribute to good soil structure and fertility.", "target_cot_step_prefi