{"id": "MCAS_2004_9_15-v1", "question": "Which of the following is the primary difference between hydraulic and pneumatic systems?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): Hydraulic systems are under pressure and pneumatic systems are not.", "B): Hydraulic systems involve liquids and pneumatic systems involve gases.", "C): Hydraulic systems are open systems and pneumatic systems are closed systems.", "D): Hydraulic systems involve fluids in motion and pneumatic systems involve fluids at rest."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. Hydraulic systems use liquids (usually oil) to transmit power, while pneumatic systems use gases (usually air) to transmit power.\n2. Both hydraulic and pneumatic systems can be either open or closed systems, depending on their design and application.\n3. Hydraulic systems involve fluids in motion (the liquid is pumped through the system), while pneumatic systems involve fluids at rest (the gas is compressed and stored in a reservoir).", "initial_cot_probs": [1.4374350598700403e-07, 2.4173938072635792e-05, 9.189214722482575e-09, 4.118320262591624e-08], "initial_probs": [4.1711846279213205e-06, 0.0003313582274131477, 3.423917007694399e-07, 2.23267420551565e-06], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "MCAS_2004_9_15-v1_step_0", "global_job_index": 907, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Hydraulic systems use liquids (usually oil) to transmit power, while pneumatic systems use gases (usually air) to transmit power.", "2.", "Both hydraulic and pneumatic systems can be either open or closed systems, depending on their design and application.", "3.", "Hydraulic systems involve fluids in motion (the liquid is pumped through the system), while pneumatic systems involve fluids at rest (the gas is compressed and stored in a reservoir)."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "MCAS_2004_9_15-v1_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=