{"id": "MDSA_2007_8_17", "question": "A student has one liter of feathers and one liter of iron nails. Which statement best compares the masses of the two samples?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): The masses cannot be compared without a balance.", "B): The mass of the feathers is less than the mass of the nails.", "C): The mass of the feathers is the same as the mass of the nails.", "D): The mass of the feathers is greater than the mass of the nails."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. We know that both samples have the same volume (one liter).\n2. Feathers are less dense than iron nails.\n3. Density is mass divided by volume.\n4. Since the volume is the same for both samples, the one with the higher density will have a greater mass.\n5. Iron nails have a higher density than feathers.\n6. Therefore, the mass of the iron nails is greater than the mass of the feathers.", "initial_cot_probs": [8.701767484353695e-08, 1.8790586182149127e-05, 1.9416267704741585e-08, 1.6257041579592624e-07], "initial_probs": [5.528574183699675e-05, 0.00031814753310754895, 0.00017029207083396614, 3.353250212967396e-05], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "MDSA_2007_8_17_step_1", "global_job_index": 1767, "cot_step": "We know that both samples have the same volume (one liter).", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "We know that both samples have the same volume (one liter).", "2.", "Feathers are less dense than iron nails.", "3.", "Density is mass divided by volume.", "4.", "Since the volume is the same for both samples, the one with the higher density will have a greater mass.", "5.", "Iron nails have a higher density than feathers.", "6.", "Therefore, the mass of the iron nails is greater than the mass of the feathers."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "MDSA_2007_8_17_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/MDSA_2007_8_17_s