{"id": "Mercury_400699", "question": "A student mixes vinegar and baking soda to use in a volcano model. The mixture causes the volcano model to feel cool when it is touched. What energy transformation has taken place?", "step_idx": 2, "options": ["A): light energy changed to heat energy", "B): heat energy changed to chemical energy", "C): chemical energy changed to heat energy", "D): chemical energy changed to light energy"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The student mixes vinegar (acetic acid) and baking soda (sodium bicarbonate), which are both chemical substances.\n2. When these two substances react, they undergo a chemical reaction that produces carbon dioxide gas, water, and a salt (sodium acetate).\n3. The reaction is exothermic, meaning it releases heat energy into the surroundings.\n4. The volcano model feels cool when touched because the heat energy released by the reaction is absorbed by the surrounding air and the model itself, causing a decrease in temperature.", "initial_cot_probs": [5.3013682332903045e-08, 9.904260167559187e-08, 4.5276799937710166e-05, 2.2099390761809445e-08], "initial_probs": [2.847887344614719e-06, 7.74135969550116e-06, 0.0006968550151214004, 6.831726295786211e-06], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "Mercury_400699_step_2", "global_job_index": 851, "cot_step": "2.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The student mixes vinegar (acetic acid) and baking soda (sodium bicarbonate), which are both chemical substances.", "2.", "When these two substances react, they undergo a chemical reaction that produces carbon dioxide gas, water, and a salt (sodium acetate).", "3.", "The reaction is exothermic, meaning it releases heat energy into the surroundings.", "4.", "The volcano model feels cool when touched because the heat energy released by the reaction is absorbed by the surrounding air and the model itself, causing a decrease in temperature."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id":