{"id": "Mercury_7252088", "question": "Which action explains how a somatic cell mutation can harm an organism?", "step_idx": 5, "options": ["A): creating a dominant allele", "B): affecting gamete formation", "C): leading to tumors in tissue", "D): being passed on to offspring"], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. Somatic cell mutations occur in non-reproductive cells of an organism.\n2. These mutations can affect the function of the cell in which they occur.\n3. If the mutation disrupts normal cell function, it can lead to abnormal cell growth or division.\n4. Abnormal cell growth can result in the formation of tumors in tissues.", "initial_cot_probs": [4.3621626311107775e-09, 2.334897164502081e-09, 3.119359098491259e-05, 7.580300831477871e-10], "initial_probs": [8.288187700600247e-07, 5.027039833294111e-07, 0.0004293387464713305, 3.91506262076291e-07], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7252088_step_5", "global_job_index": 1485, "cot_step": "If the mutation disrupts normal cell function, it can lead to abnormal cell growth or division.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Somatic cell mutations occur in non-reproductive cells of an organism.", "2.", "These mutations can affect the function of the cell in which they occur.", "3.", "If the mutation disrupts normal cell function, it can lead to abnormal cell growth or division.", "4.", "Abnormal cell growth can result in the formation of tumors in tissues."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7252088_step_5", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_7252088_step_5.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7252088", "step_idx": 5, "target_index": 191, "global_job_index": 1485, "question": "Which act