{"id": "Mercury_7136885", "question": "Some scientists predict that as greenhouse gases change the climate of Earth, the number and strength of hurricanes will increase. In order for this to occur, the climate change would have to affect Earth by changing the", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): depths of the oceans.", "B): speed of currents in the oceans.", "C): chemical compositions of the oceans.", "D): amount of dissolved oxygen in the oceans."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The question is about the relationship between climate change and the number and strength of hurricanes.\n2. Hurricanes are fueled by warm ocean waters.\n3. Climate change can lead to warmer ocean temperatures.\n4. Warmer ocean temperatures can provide more energy for hurricanes, potentially increasing their number and strength.\n5. The question asks which aspect of the climate change would have to change to affect hurricanes.", "initial_cot_probs": [3.3965393413382117e-06, 1.0462077625561506e-05, 2.33440528063511e-06, 3.329850173372506e-08], "initial_probs": [2.2825108317192644e-05, 0.00014883838593959808, 2.2825108317192644e-05, 3.5003433822566876e-06], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7136885_step_1", "global_job_index": 393, "cot_step": "The question is about the relationship between climate change and the number and strength of hurricanes.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The question is about the relationship between climate change and the number and strength of hurricanes.", "2.", "Hurricanes are fueled by warm ocean waters.", "3.", "Climate change can lead to warmer ocean temperatures.", "4.", "Warmer ocean temperatures can provide more energy for hurricanes, potentially increasing their number and strength.", "5.", "The question asks which aspect of the climate change would have to change to affect hurricanes."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7136885_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapte