{"id": "Mercury_403234", "question": "A 20 N object is placed on a surface and starts to slide. What is the most likely reason the object begins to move?", "step_idx": 3, "options": ["A): Gravity exerts a balanced force on the object.", "B): An unbalanced force causes acceleration.", "C): Friction is applied to the object.", "D): The forces acting on the object are in equilibrium."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. Gravity exerts a downward force on the object, which is given as 20 N.\n2. The object starts to slide, which means it is not in equilibrium.\n3. For an object to start moving, there must be an unbalanced force acting on it.\n4. Friction is a force that opposes the motion of an object.\n5. Since the object is sliding, it means that the force of friction is not enough to counteract the force of gravity.\n6. Therefore, the most likely reason the object begins to move is that an unbalanced force causes acceleration.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.645406338430689e-09, 2.1435947928694077e-05, 4.942269260510557e-09, 4.056861790946442e-10], "initial_probs": [3.517444113754209e-08, 7.20647003618069e-05, 1.8220811398350634e-05, 2.0241492393324734e-07], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_403234_step_3", "global_job_index": 1491, "cot_step": "3.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Gravity exerts a downward force on the object, which is given as 20 N.\n2.", "The object starts to slide, which means it is not in equilibrium.", "3.", "For an object to start moving, there must be an unbalanced force acting on it.", "4.", "Friction is a force that opposes the motion of an object.", "5.", "Since the object is sliding, it means that the force of friction is not enough to counteract the force of gravity.", "6.", "Therefore, the most likely reason the object begins to move is that an unbalanced force causes acceleration."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_403234_step_3", "adapter_path": "../../../../