{"id": "Mercury_412202", "question": "Students heated three objects to different temperatures during a classroom demonstration. Each object emitted light of a different color as shown below. Object 1: blue light Object 2: red light Object 3: orange light Which list presents the objects in order from highest to lowest temperature?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): Object 1, Object 2, Object 3", "B): Object 1, Object 3, Object 2", "C): Object 2, Object 1, Object 3", "D): Object 2, Object 3, Object 1"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The color of light emitted by an object is related to its temperature.\n2. Blue light has a shorter wavelength and higher frequency than red or orange light.\n3. Objects emitting blue light have higher temperatures than those emitting red or orange light.", "initial_cot_probs": [7.399782771244645e-05, 4.40007084989702e-07, 2.6687780518841464e-07, 8.059011236127844e-09], "initial_probs": [0.0017982404679059982, 0.00045466635492630303, 0.00016726239118725061, 0.0001476085453759879], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "Mercury_412202_step_1", "global_job_index": 1075, "cot_step": "The color of light emitted by an object is related to its temperature.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The color of light emitted by an object is related to its temperature.", "2.", "Blue light has a shorter wavelength and higher frequency than red or orange light.", "3.", "Objects emitting blue light have higher temperatures than those emitting red or orange light."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_412202_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_412202_step_1.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_412202", "step_idx": 1, "target_i