ir cores.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: A red giant star differs from main sequence stars because it\n\nChoices:\n(A): burns at a cooler temperature.\n(B): is always larger than other suns.\n(C): has greater density and gravity.\n(D): fuses hydrogen to make helium.\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\n1.\nA red giant star is a phase in the life cycle of a star that occurs after it has exhausted the hydrogen fuel in its core.\n2.\nDuring this phase, the star expands and cools, which gives it a reddish appearance.\n3.", "specificity_preds": [], "specificity_probs": [], "new_cot": "", "new_cot_probs": [], "cot_prob": [-0.5086631178855896], "cot_step_prob": [-0.5101713538169861]}}}
{"id": "Mercury_SC_401792", "question": "Which is a renewable resource?", "step_idx": 7, "options": ["A): oil", "B): coal", "C): trees", "D): aluminum"], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. A renewable resource is a natural resource that can be replenished or regenerated over time.\n2. Oil and coal are fossil fuels, which are non-renewable resources because they take millions of years to form and cannot be replenished within a human lifetime.\n3. Aluminum is a metal that is extracted from bauxite ore, which is a non-renewable resource.\n4. Trees are a renewable resource because they can be replanted and regrown over time.", "initial_cot_probs": [4.942597886525846e-09, 2.3347179745059066e-09, 4.005028313258663e-05, 2.64558219775779e-09], "initial_probs": [3.455563444276777e-07, 9.393194773110736e-07, 0.0007079690112732351, 5.027814609093184e-07], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "Mercury_SC_401792_step_7", "global_job_index": 297, "cot_step": "Trees are a renewable resource because they can be replanted and regrown over time.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "A renewable resource is a natural resource that can be replenished or regenerated over time.", "2.", "Oil and coal are fossil fuels, which are non-renewable resources because they take millions of years to form and cannot be replenished within a human lifetime.", "3.", "Aluminum is a metal that is extracted from bauxite ore, which is a non-renewable resource.", "4.", "Trees are a renewable resource because they can be replanted and regrown over time."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_SC_401792_step_7", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_SC_401792_step_7.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "M