{"id": "MCAS_2003_8_31", "question": "On a hot day, Jenny walked home from the grocery store with a bag of chocolate chips. When she arrived home the chocolate chips had melted in the bag. Why did the chocolate chips melt?", "step_idx": 2, "options": ["A): Heat transferred from the chocolate chips to the bag.", "B): Heat evaporated from the bag to the chocolate chips.", "C): Heat transferred from the environment to the chocolate chips.", "D): Heat condensed from her hand to the chocolate chips."], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. Jenny walked home on a hot day, which means the environment was warm.\n2. The chocolate chips were in a bag, which is an insulator and does not directly transfer heat.\n3. The chocolate chips melted, which means they absorbed heat.", "initial_cot_probs": [8.283854526780488e-07, 3.211999199947968e-08, 0.00012294329644646496, 6.324801127277624e-09], "initial_probs": [2.115316419804003e-05, 9.294051892538846e-07, 0.0008994553936645389, 5.637127173940826e-07], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "MCAS_2003_8_31_step_2", "global_job_index": 243, "cot_step": "2.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Jenny walked home on a hot day, which means the environment was warm.", "2.", "The chocolate chips were in a bag, which is an insulator and does not directly transfer heat.", "3.", "The chocolate chips melted, which means they absorbed heat."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "MCAS_2003_8_31_step_2", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/MCAS_2003_8_31_step_2.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "MCAS_2003_8_31", "step_idx": 2, "target_index": 29, "global_job_index": 243, "question": "On a hot day, Jenny walked home from the grocery store with a bag of cho