{"id": "TIMSS_2011_8_pg102", "question": "Robert put two drops of an indicator into vinegar, and the color turned red. He then added drops of ammonia solution until the color disappeared. What process occurred?", "step_idx": 7, "options": ["A): rusting", "B): melting", "C): evaporation", "D): neutralization"], "correct": "D", "initial_cot": "1. Robert put two drops of an indicator into vinegar, and the color turned red. This indicates that the vinegar is acidic.\n2. He then added drops of ammonia solution until the color disappeared. Ammonia is a base.\n3. The disappearance of the color suggests that the acidic vinegar and basic ammonia solution reacted with each other.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.1028447044481027e-09, 2.9978426407950565e-09, 9.732570305232002e-10, 1.891845022328198e-05], "initial_probs": [2.8413271735416856e-08, 1.2733944743104075e-07, 3.2196453503274824e-08, 0.0001582381228217855], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 3, "adapter_id": "TIMSS_2011_8_pg102_step_7", "global_job_index": 775, "cot_step": "The disappearance of the color suggests that the acidic vinegar and basic ammonia solution reacted with each other.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Robert put two drops of an indicator into vinegar, and the color turned red.", "This indicates that the vinegar is acidic.", "2.", "He then added drops of ammonia solution until the color disappeared.", "Ammonia is a base.", "3.", "The disappearance of the color suggests that the acidic vinegar and basic ammonia solution reacted with each other."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "TIMSS_2011_8_pg102_step_7", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/TIMSS_2011_8_pg102_step_7.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "TIMSS_2011_8_pg102