{"id": "AKDE&ED_2008_8_53", "question": "Which statement explains why most salmon leave salt water and return to fresh water?", "step_idx": 6, "options": ["A): It is a learned behavior that maintains the population.", "B): It is a learned behavior that maintains salt concentrations.", "C): It is an inherited behavior that maintains the population.", "D): It is an inherited behavior that maintains salt concentrations."], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. Salmon are known to migrate from salt water to fresh water and back.\n2. This behavior is not learned but rather instinctual, as salmon are born in fresh water and migrate to the ocean to grow before returning to fresh water to spawn.\n3. The purpose of this migration is to reproduce, which helps maintain the salmon population.\n4. The migration does not directly maintain salt concentrations in the water.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.3518563264369732e-06, 5.939642022667613e-08, 5.7482389820506796e-05, 1.1096712171365652e-07], "initial_probs": [1.9062223145738244e-05, 9.004355888464488e-06, 0.00012430132483132184, 0.0008105463930405676], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "AKDE&ED_2008_8_53_step_6", "global_job_index": 671, "cot_step": "4.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Salmon are known to migrate from salt water to fresh water and back.", "2.", "This behavior is not learned but rather instinctual, as salmon are born in fresh water and migrate to the ocean to grow before returning to fresh water to spawn.", "3.", "The purpose of this migration is to reproduce, which helps maintain the salmon population.", "4.", "The migration does not directly maintain salt concentrations in the water."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "AKDE&ED_2008_8_53_step_6", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/AKDE&ED_2008_8_53_step_6.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Ph