{"id": "Mercury_400877", "question": "What is the mass of a carbon atom that has 6 protons, 7 neutrons, and 6 electrons?", "step_idx": 7, "options": ["A): 6", "B): 7", "C): 13", "D): 19"], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. The mass of a proton is approximately 1 atomic mass unit (amu).\n2. The mass of a neutron is also approximately 1 amu.\n3. The mass of an electron is negligible compared to the mass of protons and neutrons (approximately 0 amu).\n4. The mass of a carbon atom with 6 protons, 7 neutrons, and 6 electrons is the sum of the masses of its protons and neutrons.\n5. So, the mass of this carbon atom is (6 protons * 1 amu/proton) + (7 neutrons * 1 amu/neutron) = 6 amu + 7 amu = 13 amu.", "initial_cot_probs": [4.1292150143590334e-08, 1.2718876973849547e-07, 3.99615200876724e-05, 5.588284501811813e-09], "initial_probs": [1.3630586181534454e-05, 4.75754241051618e-05, 0.0008432945469394326, 1.5445479220943525e-05], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "Mercury_400877_step_7", "global_job_index": 1477, "cot_step": "The mass of a carbon atom with 6 protons, 7 neutrons, and 6 electrons is the sum of the masses of its protons and neutrons.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The mass of a proton is approximately 1 atomic mass unit (amu).", "2.", "The mass of a neutron is also approximately 1 amu.", "3.", "The mass of an electron is negligible compared to the mass of protons and neutrons (approximately 0 amu).", "4.", "The mass of a carbon atom with 6 protons, 7 neutrons, and 6 electrons is the sum of the masses of its protons and neutrons.", "5.", "So, the mass of this carbon atom is (6 protons * 1 amu/proton) + (7 neutrons * 1 amu/neutron) = 6 amu + 7 amu = 13 amu."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_400877_step_7", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_400877_step_7.pt", "metadata": {"base_