{"id": "Mercury_7216248", "question": "Which structures are common to both plant and animal cells?", "step_idx": 10, "options": ["A): vacuole, chloroplast, nucleus", "B): cell membrane, nucleus, mitochondrion", "C): nucleus, cell wall, cell membrane", "D): mitochondrion, vacuole, cell wall"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. We need to identify the structures that are common to both plant and animal cells.\n2. We can eliminate choices that include structures unique to plant cells only.\n3. The cell wall is unique to plant cells, so we can eliminate choice (C).\n4. Chloroplasts are also unique to plant cells, so we can eliminate choice (A).\n5. Vacuoles are present in both plant and animal cells, but they are much larger in plant cells.\n6. The nucleus and mitochondrion are present in both plant and animal cells.\n7. The cell membrane is present in both plant and animal cells.", "initial_cot_probs": [7.186474526577058e-09, 3.531985930749215e-05, 2.6437563249714913e-09, 3.649592628107712e-08], "initial_probs": [3.9163901988104044e-07, 0.0004294843238312751, 3.4562023643047723e-07, 5.698313998436788e-07], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7216248_step_10", "global_job_index": 877, "cot_step": "6.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "We need to identify the structures that are common to both plant and animal cells.", "2.", "We can eliminate choices that include structures unique to plant cells only.", "3.", "The cell wall is unique to plant cells, so we can eliminate choice (C).", "4.", "Chloroplasts are also unique to plant cells, so we can eliminate choice (A).", "5.", "Vacuoles are present in both plant and animal cells, but they are much larger in plant cells.", "6.", "The nucleus and mitochondrion are present in both plant and animal cells.", "7.", "The cell membrane is present in both plant and animal cells."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7216248_step_10", "adapter_path": "../../