{"id": "Mercury_183820", "question": "Which element below is found in the smallest quantity in most living things?", "step_idx": 9, "options": ["A): iron", "B): carbon", "C): nitrogen", "D): hydrogen"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. We need to determine which element is found in the smallest quantity in most living things.\n2. We can eliminate options (B) and (C) because carbon and nitrogen are essential elements for life and are present in large quantities in living organisms.\n3. Now we need to compare iron (A) and hydrogen (D).\n4. Hydrogen is the most abundant element in living organisms, as it is a part of water (H2O) and organic molecules.\n5. Iron, on the other hand, is required in smaller amounts for various biological processes, such as oxygen transport in hemoglobin.", "initial_cot_probs": [6.0229795053601265e-06, 4.8468900004650095e-09, 6.223530579774206e-09, 1.1031472268996367e-07], "initial_probs": [0.00024955911794677377, 2.630333801789675e-05, 2.3212614905787632e-05, 0.00022023516066838056], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "Mercury_183820_step_9", "global_job_index": 1719, "cot_step": "Iron, on the other hand, is required in smaller amounts for various biological processes, such as oxygen transport in hemoglobin.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "We need to determine which element is found in the smallest quantity in most living things.", "2.", "We can eliminate options (B) and (C) because carbon and nitrogen are essential elements for life and are present in large quantities in living organisms.", "3.", "Now we need to compare iron (A) and hydrogen (D).", "4.", "Hydrogen is the most abundant element in living organisms, as it is a part of water (H2O) and organic molecules.", "5.", "Iron, on the other hand, is required in smaller amounts for various biological processes, such as oxygen transport in hemoglobin."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_183820_step_9", "adapter_pa