{"id": "Mercury_400407", "question": "Which statement is true about the solar system?", "step_idx": 7, "options": ["A): The gas planets are closer to the Sun.", "B): The solid planets are closer to the Sun.", "C): The planets are arranged in order of increasing size.", "D): The solid planets are much larger than the gas planets."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The gas planets (Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune) are farther from the Sun than the solid planets (Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars).\n2. The solid planets are closer to the Sun than the gas planets.\n3. The planets are arranged in order of increasing distance from the Sun, not by size.\n4. The solid planets are not much larger than the gas planets; in fact, the gas planets are much larger.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.8471531859631796e-07, 1.6627542208880186e-05, 3.833644068862441e-09, 1.8108851085330002e-09], "initial_probs": [1.3334529285202734e-05, 0.00018407750758342445, 4.329088369559031e-06, 1.1767681826313492e-05], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_400407_step_7", "global_job_index": 1181, "cot_step": "The solid planets are not much larger than the gas planets; in fact, the gas planets are much larger.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The gas planets (Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune) are farther from the Sun than the solid planets (Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars).", "2.", "The solid planets are closer to the Sun than the gas planets.", "3.", "The planets are arranged in order of increasing distance from the Sun, not by size.", "4.", "The solid planets are not much larger than the gas planets; in fact, the gas planets are much larger."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_400407_step_7", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s1/Mercury_400407_step_7.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct