{"id": "Mercury_409301", "question": "The gravitational pull between the Moon and Earth affects conditions here on Earth even though the Moon has about 1/80 the mass and about 1/4 the diameter of Earth. If the Moon was about the same size and mass of Earth, which would most likely occur?", "step_idx": 6, "options": ["A): There would be smaller tides on Earth.", "B): There would be bigger tides on Earth.", "C): Objects would weigh more on Earth.", "D): Objects would weigh less on Earth."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The gravitational pull between two objects depends on their masses and the distance between them.\n2. The Moon has about 1/80 the mass of Earth and about 1/4 the diameter.\n3. If the Moon was about the same size and mass as Earth, the distance between the two would be much greater.\n4. A greater distance would result in a weaker gravitational pull between the two objects.\n5. The gravitational pull between the Moon and Earth is responsible for the tides on Earth.\n6. If the gravitational pull was weaker, the tides on Earth would be smaller.", "initial_cot_probs": [5.139399945619516e-05, 3.649870095046026e-08, 8.143960172901643e-09, 1.102165247957032e-09], "initial_probs": [5.113070801598951e-05, 0.0002942369319498539, 6.565312651218846e-05, 1.6599711671005934e-05], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "Mercury_409301_step_6", "global_job_index": 941, "cot_step": "4.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The gravitational pull between two objects depends on their masses and the distance between them.", "2.", "The Moon has about 1/80 the mass of Earth and about 1/4 the diameter.", "3.", "If the Moon was about the same size and mass as Earth, the distance between the two would be much greater.", "4.", "A greater distance would result in a weaker gravitational pull between the two objects.", "5.", "The gravitational pull between the Moon and Earth is responsible for the tides on Earth.", "6.", "If the gravitational pull was weaker, the tides on Ea