{"id": "Mercury_7218820", "question": "On August 21, a flash flood warning was issued for the Las Vegas area. Which statement best describes this warning in terms of weather and climate?", "step_idx": 9, "options": ["A): It is a constant climate feature throughout the year.", "B): It is a seasonal weather feature with irregular occurrences.", "C): It is a continuous weather feature during the season in which it occurs.", "D): It is a rare event inconsistent with local climate and weather."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. A flash flood warning is a specific weather event, not a climate feature.\n2. Flash floods can occur in any season, but they are more common in areas with heavy rainfall.\n3. The Las Vegas area is known for its desert climate, which typically has low rainfall.\n4. The occurrence of a flash flood warning in Las Vegas is not a constant feature throughout the year.\n5. Flash floods are not continuous weather features; they are sudden and unpredictable.\n6. The statement that best describes the flash flood warning in terms of weather and climate is (D): It is a rare event inconsistent with local climate and weather.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.5187524127213692e-08, 9.903509834430224e-08, 1.720971987140274e-08, 2.7459687771624885e-05], "initial_probs": [9.483552787514782e-08, 9.177948959404603e-05, 1.0961495718220249e-05, 5.566706749959849e-05], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 3, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7218820_step_9", "global_job_index": 711, "cot_step": "Flash floods are not continuous weather features; they are sudden and unpredictable.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "A flash flood warning is a specific weather event, not a climate feature.", "2.", "Flash floods can occur in any season, but they are more common in areas with heavy rainfall.", "3.", "The Las Vegas area is known for its desert climate, which typically has low rainfall.", "4.", "The occurrence of a flash flood warning in Las Vegas is not a constant feature throughout the year.", "5.", "