{"id": "Mercury_SC_415762", "question": "A car is rolling on a level street. What can make the car stop moving?", "step_idx": 7, "options": ["A): a force that pushes straight up", "B): a force that pushes straight down", "C): a force that pushes the same direction that the car is moving", "D): a force that pushes the opposite of the direction that the car is moving"], "correct": "D", "initial_cot": "1. A force that pushes straight up (A) will not affect the car's horizontal motion, as it is perpendicular to the direction of motion.\n2. A force that pushes straight down (B) also will not affect the car's horizontal motion, as it is perpendicular to the direction of motion.\n3. A force that pushes the same direction that the car is moving (C) will only increase the car's speed, not stop it.\n4. A force that pushes the opposite of the direction that the car is moving (D) will act against the car's motion and can eventually bring it to a stop.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.2142664590774075e-08, 1.954083295174769e-08, 4.360149574722527e-09, 6.600635242648423e-05], "initial_probs": [4.434486697846296e-07, 1.0637781997502316e-06, 2.6896523763753066e-07, 0.00033422914566472173], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 3, "adapter_id": "Mercury_SC_415762_step_7", "global_job_index": 375, "cot_step": "A force that pushes the opposite of the direction that the car is moving (D) will act against the car's motion and can eventually bring it to a stop.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "A force that pushes straight up (A) will not affect the car's horizontal motion, as it is perpendicular to the direction of motion.", "2.", "A force that pushes straight down (B) also will not affect the car's horizontal motion, as it is perpendicular to the direction of motion.", "3.", "A force that pushes the same direction that the car is moving (C) will only increase the car's speed, not stop it.", "4.", "A force that pushes the opposite of the direction that the car is moving (D) will act against the car's mo