{"id": "Mercury_7064575", "question": "Coal-powered plants are designed specifically to convert", "step_idx": 15, "options": ["A): electrical energy to heat energy.", "B): chemical energy to electrical energy.", "C): electrical energy to radiant energy.", "D): kinetic energy to potential energy."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. Coal-powered plants are a type of power plant that uses coal as a fuel source.\n2. The primary purpose of a power plant is to generate electricity.\n3. Electricity is a form of energy that can be converted into other forms of energy.\n4. Coal contains chemical energy, which is released when it is burned.\n5. The burning of coal in a power plant generates heat energy.\n6. The heat energy is then used to produce steam, which drives a turbine.\n7. The turbine is connected to a generator, which converts the mechanical energy of the spinning turbine into electrical energy.\n8. Therefore, coal-powered plants are designed specifically to convert chemical energy (from coal) to electrical energy.", "initial_cot_probs": [5.904042810200849e-10, 5.42109000889468e-06, 5.904042810200849e-10, 6.2228146247012e-11], "initial_probs": [3.04911651483053e-07, 9.58003947744146e-05, 1.1217072426461527e-07, 2.8361201387383517e-08], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7064575_step_15", "global_job_index": 391, "cot_step": "Therefore, coal-powered plants are designed specifically to convert chemical energy (from coal) to electrical energy.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Coal-powered plants are a type of power plant that uses coal as a fuel source.", "2.", "The primary purpose of a power plant is to generate electricity.", "3.", "Electricity is a form of energy that can be converted into other forms of energy.", "4.", "Coal contains chemical energy, which is released when it is burned.", "5.", "The burning of coal in a power plant generates heat energy.", "6.", "The heat energy is then used to produce steam, which drives a turbine.", "7.", "Th